# `skills add` mirrors the kmp-* skills as symlinks — committing those would only ship broken
# links. Ignore the vendored ones by name, wherever they land: they are reproducible from
# skills-lock.json, so losing them costs a re-sync.
#
# The awake-* skills under .agents/skills/ are NOT vendored (skills-lock.json has 70 entries and
# none are awake-*) and are tracked. A blanket `.agents/skills/` ignore used to cover them, which
# left 26 first-party skill directories -- the ones CLAUDE.md cites as this project's
# architectural rules -- existing in no commit and recoverable from nothing.
skills/kmp-*
.agents/skills/kmp-*
.artifacts/
.codex/
.DS_Store
build/
/captures
.externalNativeBuild
.cxx
awake-demo/iosApp/Podfile.lock
awake-demo/iosApp/Pods/*
awake-demo/iosApp/iosApp.xcworkspace/*
awake-demo/iosApp/iosApp.xcodeproj/*
!awake-demo/iosApp/iosApp.xcodeproj/project.pbxproj
samples/hello-cube/iosApp/iosApp.xcworkspace/*
samples/hello-cube/iosApp/iosApp.xcodeproj/*
!samples/hello-cube/iosApp/iosApp.xcodeproj/project.pbxproj
shared/shared.podspec
/awake/backend/vulkan/build-native/*
.playwright-mcp/
.webui_secret_key
/third_party/
**/karma.config.d/awake-serve-test-resources.js
# syncAwakeShaders' output. It copies the canonical WGSL from a module's own shader source
# directory into the per-backend resource trees each loader reads, so everything below is a
# copy of a file already tracked elsewhere -- regenerated by the task on demand, and committing
# it only dirties the working tree on every build. Nothing is compiled any more (both backends
# consume WGSL), so there is no artifact here a checkout would be missing.
/awake/asset/shaders/src/appMain/
/awake/asset/shaders/src/wasmJsMain/
/awake/asset/shader-pack/src/appMain/
/awake/asset/shader-pack/src/wasmJsMain/
/samples/*/src/appMain/resources/assets/shader/
/samples/*/src/wasmJsMain/resources/assets/shader/

# JVM crash dumps -- a headless Vulkan test that aborts drops these beside the module.
hs_err_pid*.log
replay_pid*.log
